/-!
# Counterexamples for randomization-based g-estimation in the RPSFTM

Concrete trials in which exactly one assumption of the RPSFTM fails and the mean-form
g-estimating function (`CausalInference.StructuralNested.SwitchingTrial.gMean`) misses the
treatment effect, plus the non-identification and multiple root phenomena that the treatment
switching documents report.

All trials live on the eight point space `Bool × Bool × Bool` with the uniform measure
(`CausalInference.Mediation.Counterexample.μ₀`): the first coordinate is the randomized arm, the
other two are a prognostic type independent of it. Times are scaled by the prognostic type
`s = 1` or `s = 2`, so the untreated time is not constant.

## Main results

* `NonCommon.root`: **failure of the common treatment effect** (TSD 16, Sections 3.2.2 and
  3.3.1). Experimental patients have time ratio `1/2`, the control switcher `4/5`; randomization
  holds and no common `ψ` fits the data (`NonCommon.not_commonEffect`), and the unique root of the
  mean-form equation has time ratio `exp ψ̂ = 20/43`, not `1/2`, matching the bias formula
  `SwitchingTrial.exp_root_of_armEffects`.
* `NotRandomized.root`: **failure of randomization.** The common effect holds with time ratio
  `1/2`, the arms differ in untreated prognosis (`NotRandomized.not_randomized`), and the root has
  time ratio `1/4`.
* `ActiveControl.root`: **an active comparator** (TSD 16, Section 3.3.1; TSD 24,
  Section 4.2.1.1). Time on the control treatment also halves survival time; randomization holds;
  the one-parameter model fits for no `ψ` (`ActiveControl.not_commonEffect`) and its estimating
  equation has the unique root `ψ̂ = 0` (no effect), while the experimental time ratio is `1/2`.
* `TwoParam.randomized_of_curve`: **two effects are not identified by one randomization**
  (TSD 16, Section 3.3.1; TSD 24, Section 4.2.1.1 on bivariate and stratified RPSFTMs). With the
  same observed data, every pair of time ratios `(x₁, x₂)` on the curve `2 x₁ = 1 + x₂` gives a
  two-parameter model in which the untreated time is independent of the arm; for instance
  `(1, 1)` and `(2, 3)` (`TwoParam.not_identified`).
* `Multiplier.two_roots`: **the multiplier analysis can have two roots** (TSD 24,
  Section 4.2.1.1). With `k = 1/2` in control switchers, the same observed data are consistent
  with the multiplier model, randomization included, at `ψ = 0` and at `ψ = 2 log 2`. The arm
  contrast of `T^c` is positive here, which violates the hypothesis of
  `SwitchingTrial.gMult_eq_zero_iff`.
* `Wilcoxon.multiple_roots`: **multiple roots of a rank g-test** (TSD 24, Section 4.2.1). A
  sample of two experimental and two control patients generated by the model with time ratio
  `1/2` (the untreated times agree between arms at `ψ = log (1/2)`), with a nonzero first stage,
  for which the Wilcoxon (Mann-Whitney) g-statistic for uncensored data is zero at
  `ψ = log (1/8)` and at `ψ = log (1/2)` but equals `-2` at `ψ = log (1/5)` in between. By
  `SwitchingTrial.eq_trueParam_of_armLaw_eq` this cannot happen for the population criterion of
  equal arm laws; it is a property of finite sample statistics.

## Sources

N. R. Latimer, K. R. Abrams, *NICE DSU Technical Support Document 16* (2014), Sections 3.2.2,
3.3.1, 4; H. Bell Gorrod, N. R. Latimer, K. R. Abrams, *NICE DSU Technical Support Document 24*
(2024), Sections 4.2.1 and 4.2.1.1. In `NonCommon` the experimental times are `4, 8` from
untreated `2, 4`, and one control switcher switches at time `1` with time ratio `0.8`.
-/

@[expose] public section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Set
open CausalInference.Mediation.Counterexample

namespace CausalInference

namespace StructuralNested

namespace RPSFTMCounterexample

open SwitchingTrial

/-! ### Computations on the eight point space -/

/-- The prognostic scale: `s = 2` for the good type, `1` for the poor type. -/
def scale (ω : Ω₀) : ℝ := if ω.2.1 then 2 else 1

/-- Arm means on the eight point space when the arm is the first coordinate. -/
theorem armMean_μ₀ (M : SwitchingTrial Ω₀) (hR : ∀ ω, M.R ω = ω.1) (X : Ω₀ → ℝ) (r : Bool) :
    M.armMean μ₀ X r =
      (X (r, false, false) + X (r, false, true) + X (r, true, false) + X (r, true, true)) / 4 := by
  have hs : M.arm r = {ω : Ω₀ | ω.1 = r} := by ext ω; simp [SwitchingTrial.arm, hR]
  have hcard : (Finset.univ.filter fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.1 = r).card = 4 := by cases r <;> rfl
  have hreal : μ₀.real {ω : Ω₀ | ω.1 = r} = 1 / 2 := by
    rw [μ₀_real_eq (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.1 = r), hcard]; norm_num
  rw [SwitchingTrial.armMean, ← Mediation.condMean, Mediation.condMean_eq, hs, hreal,
    ← integral_indicator (Set.toFinite _).measurableSet, integral_μ₀]
  cases r <;> simp [Fintype.sum_prod_type, Set.indicator] <;> ring

/-- Both arms have positive probability. -/
theorem arm_ne_zero (M : SwitchingTrial Ω₀) (hR : ∀ ω, M.R ω = ω.1) (r : Bool) :
    μ₀ (M.arm r) ≠ 0 :=
  μ₀_ne_zero_of_mem (ω := (r, true, true)) (by simp [SwitchingTrial.arm, hR])

/-- An untreated time that depends only on the prognostic type is independent of the arm. -/
theorem randomized_of_eq (M : SwitchingTrial Ω₀) (hR : ∀ ω, M.R ω = ω.1) (g : Bool × Bool → ℝ)
    (hU : ∀ ω, M.U ω = g ω.2) : M.Randomized μ₀ := by
  have hR' : M.R = (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.1) := funext hR
  have hU' : M.U = g ∘ (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.2) := funext hU
  rw [SwitchingTrial.Randomized, hR', hU']
  exact indepFun_A_UV.comp measurable_id (measurable_of_countable g)

/-! ### Failure of the common treatment effect -/

namespace NonCommon

/-- Experimental patients are fully treated with time ratio `1/2`: untreated `2 s`, observed
`4 s`. Control patients of the good type never switch (observed `4`); those of the poor type
switch at time `1` with time ratio `4/5` and survive to `9/4` (untreated time `2`). -/
noncomputable def trial : SwitchingTrial Ω₀ where
  R ω := ω.1
  T ω := if ω.1 then 4 * scale ω else if ω.2.1 then 4 else 9 / 4
  Te ω := if ω.1 then 4 * scale ω else if ω.2.1 then 0 else 5 / 4
  U ω := 2 * scale ω

/-- The arm specific model holds with `ψe = log (1/2)` and `ψs = log (4/5)`. -/
theorem armEffects : trial.ArmEffects (Real.log (1 / 2)) (Real.log (4 / 5)) := by
  intro ω
  obtain ⟨a, u, v⟩ := ω
  cases a <;> cases u <;> norm_num [trial, scale, Tc, Real.exp_log]

theorem randomized : trial.Randomized μ₀ :=
  randomized_of_eq trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun x ↦ 2 * if x.1 then 2 else 1) fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- No common effect fits the trial: the experimental patients force time ratio `1/2`, the
control switcher forces `4/5`. -/
theorem not_commonEffect (ψ : ℝ) : ¬ trial.CommonEffect ψ := by
  intro h
  have h1 := h (true, false, false)
  have h0 := h (false, false, false)
  simp only [trial, scale, Tc] at h1 h0
  norm_num at h1 h0
  linarith

/-- The mean-form estimating function is `(43 exp ψ - 20) / 8`. -/
theorem gMean_eq (ψ : ℝ) : trial.gMean μ₀ ψ = (43 * Real.exp ψ - 20) / 8 := by
  simp only [gMean, meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)]
  simp only [counterfactual, Tc, trial, scale]
  norm_num
  ring

/-- **Counterexample: no common effect.** The unique root of the mean-form equation has time
ratio `20/43`, not the experimental time ratio `1/2`; in particular the true experimental
parameter is not a root. -/
theorem root (ψ : ℝ) :
    (trial.gMean μ₀ ψ = 0 ↔ Real.exp ψ = 20 / 43) ∧ trial.gMean μ₀ (Real.log (1 / 2)) ≠ 0 := by
  refine ⟨by rw [gMean_eq]; constructor <;> intro h <;> linarith, ?_⟩
  rw [gMean_eq, Real.exp_log (by norm_num)]
  norm_num

/-- The root agrees with the bias formula `exp ψe - (exp ψs - exp ψe) E[T^e | R = 0] /
(E[T^e | R = 1] - E[T^e | R = 0]) = 1/2 - (3/10) (5/8) / (43/8) = 20/43`. -/
theorem bias_formula :
    (1 / 2 : ℝ) - (4 / 5 - 1 / 2) * trial.armMean μ₀ trial.Te false /
      trial.meanContrast μ₀ trial.Te = 20 / 43 := by
  simp only [meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)]
  simp only [trial, scale]
  norm_num

end NonCommon

/-! ### Failure of randomization -/

namespace NotRandomized

/-- The common effect holds with time ratio `1/2`, but experimental patients have untreated time
`4 s` and control patients `2 s`; nobody in control switches. -/
noncomputable def trial : SwitchingTrial Ω₀ where
  R ω := ω.1
  T ω := if ω.1 then 8 * scale ω else 2 * scale ω
  Te ω := if ω.1 then 8 * scale ω else 0
  U ω := if ω.1 then 4 * scale ω else 2 * scale ω

theorem commonEffect : trial.CommonEffect (Real.log (1 / 2)) := by
  intro ω
  obtain ⟨a, u, v⟩ := ω
  simp only [Real.exp_log (show (0 : ℝ) < 1 / 2 by norm_num)]
  cases a <;> cases u <;> norm_num [trial, Tc, scale]

/-- Randomization fails: the arm means of the untreated time are `6` and `3`. -/
theorem not_randomized : ¬ trial.Randomized μ₀ := by
  intro h
  have := meanContrast_U_of_randomized (M := trial) (μ := μ₀) (measurable_of_countable _) h
    Integrable.of_finite (arm_ne_zero trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) true)
    (arm_ne_zero trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) false)
  simp only [meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)] at this
  simp only [trial, scale] at this
  norm_num at this

/-- **Counterexample: no randomization.** The unique root has time ratio `1/4`, not `1/2`. -/
theorem root (ψ : ℝ) :
    (trial.gMean μ₀ ψ = 0 ↔ Real.exp ψ = 1 / 4) ∧ trial.gMean μ₀ (Real.log (1 / 2)) ≠ 0 := by
  have e : ∀ x, trial.gMean μ₀ x = 12 * Real.exp x - 3 := fun x ↦ by
    simp only [gMean, meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)]
    simp only [counterfactual, Tc, trial, scale]
    norm_num
    ring
  refine ⟨by rw [e]; constructor <;> intro h <;> linarith, ?_⟩
  rw [e, Real.exp_log (by norm_num)]
  norm_num

end NotRandomized

/-! ### An active comparator -/

namespace ActiveControl

/-- Time on the active control treatment: control patients take it for `s` before switching;
experimental patients never take it. -/
def Tctrl (ω : Ω₀) : ℝ := if ω.1 then 0 else scale ω

/-- Experimental patients are on the experimental treatment for `2 s`; control patients are on
the active control for `s`, then switch to the experimental treatment for `s`. Both treatments
halve survival time, so the untreated time is `s` for everyone. -/
noncomputable def trial : SwitchingTrial Ω₀ where
  R ω := ω.1
  T ω := 2 * scale ω
  Te ω := if ω.1 then 2 * scale ω else scale ω
  U ω := scale ω

/-- The three state model holds: `U = T^off + exp ψc Tctrl + exp ψe T^e`, with no time off both
treatments and `ψc = ψe = log (1/2)`; the control treatment is active (`ψc ≠ 0`). -/
theorem threeStateModel (ω : Ω₀) :
    trial.U ω = (trial.T ω - Tctrl ω - trial.Te ω) + Real.exp (Real.log (1 / 2)) * Tctrl ω +
      Real.exp (Real.log (1 / 2)) * trial.Te ω := by
  obtain ⟨a, u, v⟩ := ω
  rw [Real.exp_log (by norm_num)]
  cases a <;> norm_num [trial, Tctrl] <;> ring

theorem log_half_ne_zero : Real.log (1 / 2) ≠ 0 := by
  rw [one_div, Real.log_inv]; exact neg_ne_zero.2 (Real.log_pos one_lt_two).ne'

theorem randomized : trial.Randomized μ₀ :=
  randomized_of_eq trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun x ↦ if x.1 then 2 else 1) fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- The one-parameter model treating control time as "off" fits for no `ψ`. -/
theorem not_commonEffect (ψ : ℝ) : ¬ trial.CommonEffect ψ := by
  intro h
  have h0 := h (false, false, false)
  simp only [trial, scale, Tc] at h0
  norm_num at h0

/-- The first stage is nonzero: `E[T^e | R = 1] - E[T^e | R = 0] = 3/2`. -/
theorem firstStage : trial.meanContrast μ₀ trial.Te = 3 / 2 := by
  simp only [meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)]
  simp only [trial, scale]
  norm_num

/-- **Counterexample: active comparator.** The one-parameter estimating equation has the unique
root `ψ̂ = 0` (no effect), while the experimental treatment halves survival time. -/
theorem root (ψ : ℝ) : trial.gMean μ₀ ψ = 0 ↔ ψ = 0 := by
  have e : trial.gMean μ₀ ψ = 3 / 2 * Real.exp ψ - 3 / 2 := by
    simp only [gMean, meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)]
    simp only [counterfactual, Tc, trial, scale]
    norm_num
    ring
  rw [e]
  constructor
  · intro h
    have : Real.exp ψ = Real.exp 0 := by rw [Real.exp_zero]; linarith
    exact Real.exp_injective this
  · rintro rfl; simp

end ActiveControl

/-! ### Two effects and one randomization -/

namespace TwoParam

/-- Observed time off both treatments: `s` in control, `0` in the experimental arm. -/
def Tc (ω : Ω₀) : ℝ := if ω.1 then 0 else scale ω

/-- Observed time on treatment 1 (the experimental treatment): `2 s` in the experimental arm. -/
def T₁ (ω : Ω₀) : ℝ := if ω.1 then 2 * scale ω else 0

/-- Observed time on treatment 2 (switch to another treatment): `s` in control. -/
def T₂ (ω : Ω₀) : ℝ := if ω.1 then 0 else scale ω

/-- The two-parameter structural failure time model: `U = T^c + exp ψ₁ T₁ + exp ψ₂ T₂`, computed
from the observed data. -/
noncomputable def untreated (ψ₁ ψ₂ : ℝ) (ω : Ω₀) : ℝ :=
  Tc ω + Real.exp ψ₁ * T₁ ω + Real.exp ψ₂ * T₂ ω

/-- **Counterexample: two parameters are not identified.** For every pair of time ratios
`x₁, x₂ > 0` with `2 x₁ = 1 + x₂`, the untreated time of the two-parameter model at
`(log x₁, log x₂)` is independent of the arm under the same observed data. -/
theorem randomized_of_curve {x₁ x₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < x₁) (h₂ : 0 < x₂) (hc : 2 * x₁ = 1 + x₂) :
    IndepFun (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.1) (untreated (Real.log x₁) (Real.log x₂)) μ₀ := by
  have e : untreated (Real.log x₁) (Real.log x₂) =
      (fun x : Bool × Bool ↦ 2 * x₁ * if x.1 then 2 else 1) ∘ (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.2) := by
    funext ⟨a, u, v⟩
    simp only [untreated, Tc, T₁, T₂, scale, Real.exp_log h₁, Real.exp_log h₂,
      Function.comp_apply]
    cases a <;> cases u <;> norm_num <;> linarith
  rw [e]
  exact indepFun_A_UV.comp measurable_id (measurable_of_countable _)

/-- Two distinct parameter pairs, `(0, 0)` and `(log 2, log 3)`, both make the untreated time
independent of the arm, with different experimental effects. -/
theorem not_identified :
    IndepFun (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.1) (untreated 0 0) μ₀ ∧
      IndepFun (fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ ω.1) (untreated (Real.log 2) (Real.log 3)) μ₀ ∧
      (0 : ℝ) ≠ Real.log 2 := by
  refine ⟨?_, randomized_of_curve two_pos three_pos (by norm_num),
    (Real.log_pos one_lt_two).ne⟩
  simpa using randomized_of_curve one_pos one_pos (by norm_num)

end TwoParam

/-! ### Two roots of the multiplier analysis -/

namespace Multiplier

/-- Experimental patients: time off treatment `2 s`, on treatment `s`. Control patients switch
at once and are on the experimental treatment for `3 s`. The untreated time is `3 s`. -/
noncomputable def trial : SwitchingTrial Ω₀ where
  R ω := ω.1
  T ω := 3 * scale ω
  Te ω := if ω.1 then scale ω else 3 * scale ω
  U ω := 3 * scale ω

/-- The same observed data with untreated time `6 s`. -/
noncomputable def trial' : SwitchingTrial Ω₀ :=
  { trial with U := fun ω ↦ 6 * scale ω }

/-- The multiplier model with `k = 1/2` holds in `trial` at `ψ = 0`. -/
theorem model : trial.MultiplierModel (1 / 2) 0 := by
  intro ω; obtain ⟨a, u, v⟩ := ω
  cases a <;> norm_num [trial, Tc]

/-- The multiplier model with `k = 1/2` holds in `trial'` at `ψ = 2 log 2`. -/
theorem model' : trial'.MultiplierModel (1 / 2) (2 * Real.log 2) := by
  intro ω; obtain ⟨a, u, v⟩ := ω
  have e1 : Real.exp (2 * Real.log 2) = 4 := by
    rw [mul_comm, Real.exp_mul, Real.exp_log two_pos]; norm_num
  have e2 : Real.exp (1 / 2 * (2 * Real.log 2)) = 2 := by
    rw [show 1 / 2 * (2 * Real.log 2) = Real.log 2 by ring, Real.exp_log two_pos]
  cases a <;> simp only [trial', trial, Tc, scale, ite_true, ite_false, Bool.false_eq_true,
    one_mul, e1, e2] <;> split_ifs <;> norm_num

theorem randomized : trial.Randomized μ₀ :=
  randomized_of_eq trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun x ↦ 3 * if x.1 then 2 else 1) fun _ ↦ rfl

theorem randomized' : trial'.Randomized μ₀ :=
  randomized_of_eq trial' (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun x ↦ 6 * if x.1 then 2 else 1) fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- **Counterexample: the multiplier root is not unique.** With `k = 1/2`, the observed data of
`trial` and `trial'` coincide, both satisfy the multiplier model and randomization, at the
different parameters `0` and `2 log 2`; both are roots of the estimating function. The arm
contrast of `T^c` is `3 > 0`. -/
theorem two_roots :
    trial'.R = trial.R ∧ trial'.T = trial.T ∧ trial'.Te = trial.Te ∧
      trial.gMult μ₀ (1 / 2) 0 = 0 ∧ trial.gMult μ₀ (1 / 2) (2 * Real.log 2) = 0 ∧
      (0 : ℝ) ≠ 2 * Real.log 2 ∧ trial.meanContrast μ₀ trial.Tc = 3 := by
  have hm := Integrable.of_finite (μ := μ₀) (f := fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ (3 : ℝ) * scale ω)
  have hm' := Integrable.of_finite (μ := μ₀) (f := fun ω : Ω₀ ↦ (6 : ℝ) * scale ω)
  refine ⟨rfl, rfl, rfl, gMult_trueParam (measurable_of_countable _) model randomized hm
    (arm_ne_zero trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) true) (arm_ne_zero trial (fun _ ↦ rfl) false), ?_,
    by have := Real.log_pos one_lt_two; linarith, ?_⟩
  · exact gMult_trueParam (M := trial') (measurable_of_countable _) model' randomized' hm'
      (arm_ne_zero trial' (fun _ ↦ rfl) true) (arm_ne_zero trial' (fun _ ↦ rfl) false)
  · simp only [meanContrast, armMean_μ₀ trial (fun _ ↦ rfl)]
    simp only [Tc, trial, scale]
    norm_num

end Multiplier

/-! ### Multiple roots of a rank g-test -/

namespace Wilcoxon

/-- The centered Wilcoxon (Mann-Whitney) statistic for uncensored data, applied to the candidate
untreated times `T^c + exp ψ T^e` of an experimental sample `E` and a control sample `C`, each a
list of pairs `(T^c, T^e)`: `Σ_{i, j} sign (U_i(ψ) - U_j(ψ))`. It is zero when the two samples
are balanced in rank. -/
noncomputable def stat {m n : ℕ} (E : Fin m → ℝ × ℝ) (C : Fin n → ℝ × ℝ) (ψ : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ i, ∑ j, Real.sign ((E i).1 + Real.exp ψ * (E i).2 - ((C j).1 + Real.exp ψ * (C j).2))

/-- The experimental sample: `(T^c, T^e) = (2, 0)` and `(1/2, 5)`. -/
noncomputable def expSample : Fin 2 → ℝ × ℝ := ![(2, 0), (1 / 2, 5)]

/-- The control sample: `(T^c, T^e) = (3/2, 1)` and `(3/2, 3)`. -/
noncomputable def ctrlSample : Fin 2 → ℝ × ℝ := ![(3 / 2, 1), (3 / 2, 3)]

/-- The samples come from the model with time ratio `1/2`: at `ψ = log (1/2)` the untreated
times are `2` and `3` in both arms. -/
theorem untreated_at_truth :
    (fun i ↦ (expSample i).1 + 1 / 2 * (expSample i).2) = ![2, 3] ∧
      (fun j ↦ (ctrlSample j).1 + 1 / 2 * (ctrlSample j).2) = ![2, 3] := by
  constructor <;> funext i <;> fin_cases i <;> norm_num [expSample, ctrlSample]

/-- The first stage is nonzero: mean time on the experimental treatment `5/2` against `2`. -/
theorem firstStage : ((expSample 0).2 + (expSample 1).2) / 2 ≠
    ((ctrlSample 0).2 + (ctrlSample 1).2) / 2 := by
  norm_num [expSample, ctrlSample]

theorem stat_eq (x : ℝ) (hx : 0 < x) :
    stat expSample ctrlSample (Real.log x) =
      Real.sign (1 / 2 - x) + Real.sign (1 / 2 - 3 * x) + Real.sign (4 * x - 1) +
        Real.sign (2 * x - 1) := by
  simp only [stat, Fin.sum_univ_two, expSample, ctrlSample, Real.exp_log hx]
  norm_num
  ring_nf

/-- **Counterexample: multiple roots of a rank g-test** (TSD 24, Section 4.2.1). The Wilcoxon
g-statistic of this sample is zero at `ψ = log (1/8)` and at the true `ψ = log (1/2)`, but `-2`
at `ψ = log (1/5)` in between: its zero set is not an interval. -/
theorem multiple_roots :
    stat expSample ctrlSample (Real.log (1 / 8)) = 0 ∧
      stat expSample ctrlSample (Real.log (1 / 5)) = -2 ∧
      stat expSample ctrlSample (Real.log (1 / 2)) = 0 ∧
      Real.log (1 / 8) < Real.log (1 / 5) ∧ Real.log (1 / 5) < Real.log (1 / 2) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, Real.log_lt_log (by norm_num) (by norm_num),
    Real.log_lt_log (by norm_num) (by norm_num)⟩
  · rw [stat_eq _ (by norm_num), Real.sign_of_pos (by norm_num), Real.sign_of_pos (by norm_num),
      Real.sign_of_neg (by norm_num), Real.sign_of_neg (by norm_num)]
    norm_num
  · rw [stat_eq _ (by norm_num), Real.sign_of_pos (by norm_num), Real.sign_of_neg (by norm_num),
      Real.sign_of_neg (by norm_num), Real.sign_of_neg (by norm_num)]
    norm_num
  · rw [stat_eq _ (by norm_num)]
    norm_num [Real.sign_of_pos, Real.sign_of_neg]

end Wilcoxon

end RPSFTMCounterexample

end StructuralNested

end CausalInference
